    "explanation": "payment-svc v1.18.0 rolled out with a new response serializer (lines 102, 107) that renamed \"status\" to \"state\". From then on order-service cannot decode payment-svc's responses (lines 108, 116, 119, 128), which surfaces as api-gateway 502s (lines 114, 122, 133, 141, 150, 157, 164). payment-svc itself logs no errors — the break is the contract, introduced by the release. Roll back payment-svc. Red herrings: line 55 (a client sending one invalid request, rejected correctly with a 400); line 39 (a routine disk usage warning on the log volume, nowhere near full).",
